From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:26:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: hand the SIO to the boot
 loader

m1n1 finds the SIO by its "sio" alias, builds its firmware tables,
reserves its pre-loaded firmware and enables it. The J604 had no alias,
so the SIO stayed off and with it DisplayPort audio.

Add the alias and enable the SIO's mailbox and DART, as the M3 Pro HDMI
boards do. Give the T8132 SIO dma-channels = <128>: the endpoint is a
client-supplied cell, and the J604's clients name 0x64 and 0x66
(dp-audio0/1 in the ADT).

DPA1 itself stays disabled: the J604 dcpext runs the adopted M4 session
and is no component of the DRM device, so the DisplayPort audio
component has nothing to bind to until that session serves audio.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-sio.dtsi       |  7 +++++--
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi
index 5e0b80f254..f402aff336 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi
@@ -34,9 +34,10 @@
  * powered down.
  *
  * The port's audio is DPA1 (ADT dp-audio1, SIO channel 0x66, power gate DPA1,
- * the dp-audio node dcpext0 names), as on the M3 Pro HDMI port. It stays
- * disabled with the T8132 SIO (t8132-sio.dtsi), which needs boot loader
- * support for its firmware tables first.
+ * the dp-audio node dcpext0 names), as on the M3 Pro HDMI port. The SIO
+ * that carries it is enabled by the boot loader (alias below). DPA1 stays
+ * disabled until the adopted dcpext session serves audio: the dcpext is no
+ * component of the DRM device, so no audio component could bind to it yet.
  *
  * Copyright The Asahi Linux Contributors
  */
@@ -45,9 +46,20 @@
 	aliases {
 		/* m1n1 copies the ATC tunables through this alias. */
 		atcphy2 = &atcphy2;
+		/* The boot loader builds the SIO's tables and enables it by this alias. */
+		sio = &sio;
 	};
 };
 
+/* The SIO's mailbox and DART; the boot loader enables the SIO with its firmware. */
+&sio_mbox {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&dart_sio0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 /*
  * The SoC node describes ATC2 with its USB windows and is named after the
  * first of them. No USB controller uses ATC2 on this board: describe it again
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-sio.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-sio.dtsi
index 3d5034b332..ebc2e0ba8b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-sio.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-sio.dtsi
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+ OR MIT
 /*
- * T8132 SIO resources; channel layout and firmware regions require loader
- * support.
+ * T8132 SIO resources. The boot loader builds the SIO's firmware tables,
+ * reserves its firmware and enables it; the board names it with the "sio"
+ * alias.
  *
  * Every value is the J604 Apple device tree's (arm-io sio, dart-sio):
  * coprocessor window and auxiliary window, the ASC mailbox at coprocessor
@@ -41,6 +42,8 @@
 		reg = <0x3 0xade00000 0x0 0x88000>,
 		      <0x3 0xad850000 0x0 0x4000>;
 		#dma-cells = <1>;
+		/* Every endpoint a client names; DisplayPort audio uses 0x64 and 0x66 */
+		dma-channels = <128>;
 		mboxes = <&sio_mbox>;
 		iommus = <&dart_sio0 0>;
 		power-domains = <&ps_sio_cpu>;
